WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.060
Does your soul die a little every time you throw away unused food?
每当你扔掉没吃的食物时，你的灵魂是否会有点难过？

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:06.660
Mine does.
我的就会。

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:17.830
Maybe that feeling comes from growing up in South Africa, where the phrase “there are children starving in Africa” was more of an uncomfortable reminder of fact than a prayer at dinner time.
也许这种感觉来自我在南非长大的经历，在那里，“非洲有孩子在挨饿”这句话与其说是晚餐时的祷告，不如说是对现实的一种令人不安的提醒。

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:24.010
Food waste is a growing concern in the restaurant, supermarket, and supply chain industries.
食物浪费日益成为餐饮、超市和供应链行业关注的问题。

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:33.140
From technological solutions to educational campaigns, food producers and sellers are looking for ways to use more of what we’re already growing.
从技术解决方案到教育活动，食品生产商和销售商都在寻找办法，更充分地利用我们已经种出来的东西。

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:43.592
But last month, one popular New York City restaurant tried a different way: It changed its menu to exclusively offer food that would otherwise be thrown away.
但上个月，纽约市一家很受欢迎的餐厅尝试了一种不同的方式：它更换了菜单，专门供应那些原本会被扔掉的食物。

00:00:44.392 --> 00:00:56.042
For three weeks in March, Greenwich Village’s Blue Hill restaurant was renamed wastED, and served items like fried skate cartilage, a juice pulp burger, and a dumpster diver’s vegetable salad.
三月份的三周里，格林尼治村的蓝山餐厅更名为“wastED”，供应油炸鳐鱼软骨、果汁残渣汉堡和“翻垃圾箱者”蔬菜沙拉等菜品。

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:00.612
Each dish was tailor-made to raise awareness regarding food waste.
每道菜都是为提高人们对食物浪费的认识而量身定做的。

00:01:01.412 --> 00:01:15.882
A study by the Food Waste Reduction Alliance determined that the average restaurant generates 33 pounds of food waste for every $1,000 in revenue, and of that waste only 15.7% is donated or recycled.
“减少食物浪费联盟”的一项研究发现，平均每家餐厅每创造1000美元收入，就会产生33磅食物垃圾，其中只有15.7%被捐赠或回收。

00:01:16.682 --> 00:01:20.052
The remaining 84.3% is simply thrown out.
其余的84.3%被直接扔掉。

00:01:20.852 --> 00:01:28.932
Restaurants like Silo in the UK have experimented with zero-waste systems, but wastED took the concept to its logical conclusion.
像英国的 Silo 这样的餐厅尝试过零浪费系统，但 wastED 把这一理念贯彻到底。

00:01:29.732 --> 00:01:34.892
It should be noted that none of the items on wastED’s menu was technically made from garbage.
需要指出的是，wastED 菜单上的菜品严格来说没有一样是用垃圾做的。

00:01:35.692 --> 00:01:42.932
Instead, all the ingredients used were examples of meat cuts and produce that most restaurants would never consider serving.
相反，所用的食材都是大多数餐厅从来不会考虑供应的肉类部位和农产品。

00:01:43.732 --> 00:01:54.962
Things like kale ribs, fish collars, rejected sweet potatoes, and cucumber butts were all re-appropriated and, with the help of a number of good chefs, turned into excellent cuisine.
像羽衣甘蓝茎、鱼颈肉、被淘汰的红薯和黄瓜蒂这样的东西都被重新利用，并在一批优秀厨师的帮助下，变成了精美的菜肴。

00:01:55.762 --> 00:02:04.894
Though wastED received enthusiastic reviews, it was designed from the start as a short-lived experiment; Blue Hill has since returned to its regular menu.
尽管 wastED 获得了热烈的好评，但它从一开始就被设计成一次短期实验；此后蓝山餐厅已经恢复了常规菜单。

00:02:05.694 --> 00:02:14.664
Nevertheless, it serves as a reminder that there are many ways to address problems of sustainability, and that you can make an amazing meal out of almost anything.
尽管如此，它提醒我们：解决可持续性问题的方法有很多，而且几乎用任何东西都能做出一顿美味佳肴。
